DESCRIPTION:Join us for SUNDAY SWING NIGHT at Hall of the Above 🎷 Featu
 ring a new-to-HOTA band\, The doRiaN Mode! 🎷 The doRiaN Mode explores t
 he Great American Songbook as it dishes up vintage jazz\, swinging R&amp\;
 B\, and soulful ballads\, from the sounds of 1920s speakeasies and 1930s b
 ig-band swing to 1940s jump blues and the rollicking R&amp\;B of Ruth Brow
 n. Vocalist and bassist Dorian Bartley&nbsp\;leads this Petaluma-based aco
 ustic quartet featuring Robby Elfman on piano/clarinet\, Peter Graves on s
 ax\, and Tony Blake on drums.&nbsp\;Whether they’re stomping at the Savo
 y in salute to Count Basie or paying homage to R&amp\;B legend Etta James\
 , the doRiaN Mode brings elegance to classic American music. 💃🏻 Jasm
 ine Worrell\, the Bay Area’s top swing dance instructor\, will offer a c
 lass from 4:15 – 5:00 👯 Followed by live music and an open dance floo
 r until 7:00 PM 🎟️ $25 for admission includes the class — cash at t
 he door. Kids 12 and under are free. 🕺🏾 All skill levels welcome\; n
 o partner required. See you on the dance floor! #block-4fe0cb7564f6a0fb12b
